  "security_implications": "msg_allowed is the critical gating signal that permits message input into the HMAC core. Incorrect assertion (allowing messages during flush or while the engine is not ready) or incorrect deassertion (blocking valid messages) can be exploited by an attacker to inject spoofed data into the hash pipeline or to cause a denial of service, potentially leading to MAC forgery or integrity failure. The priority of hash_start_or_continue over packer_flush_done, if both are high, could allow message injection during a flush window—a security-significant edge case that may require hardening.",
